  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>\n<multiple-choice question=\"Which of these is a common way to improve performance in a real-time engine?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Using levels of detail (LODs) for distant objects\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Raising every texture to 8K\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Turning off occlusion culling\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Giving every object its own unique material\">\n</multiple-choice>\n<true-false-question question=\"Baked lighting is calculated ahead of time, so it costs little while the game runs but can't change during play.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\">\n</true-false-question>\n<self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">What would you check when importing a model from Blender into Unity or Unreal?</p>\n  <p>Scale and units, axis orientation, applied transforms, normals and smoothing, UVs (including lightmap UVs), material assignments, pivot placement, naming and collision.</p>\n</self-check>\n"
}